# FIGTR — Project Rules

These rules govern all development work in this repository, including AI-assisted development. All contributors and AI assistants MUST follow these rules.

## Documentation First

- Always read the relevant documentation before writing code.
- Consult `docs/` (Vision, Architecture, Database, API, UI, Decisions) before starting any task.
- Do not create features without a specification.

## Architecture & Code

- Follow existing architecture patterns and conventions.
- Do not introduce unnecessary dependencies. Every new dependency must be justified.
- Use environment variables for all configuration.
- Never hardcode secrets, API keys, or credentials.
- Write tests for all new functionality.
- Keep backend business logic separated from views/controllers.
- Keep frontend components reusable.
- Do not modify unrelated files. Keep changes scoped to the task at hand.

## Communication

- Explain changes after completing tasks.
- Update relevant documentation when behavior changes.

## Definition of Done

A task is complete only when:

- [ ] Code is implemented per the specification.
- [ ] Tests are written and passing.
- [ ] Code follows the project's style and conventions.
- [ ] Documentation is updated if needed.
- [ ] No unrelated files were modified.
- [ ] Changes are explained.